      "heading": "Ratios, safeguarding and the premises walk",
      "html": "<p>Much of the evidence a nursery needs lives in the moment, not at a desk. The staff-to-child ratio at the busiest part of the day, the fire exit that was clear, the outdoor space that was checked before children used it, the sleep and nappy routines observed, the entrance that was secure. Captured later from memory, these become claims. Captured at the point of observation, with a photo and a timestamp, they become evidence.</p><p>Safeguarding needs care and honesty here. Quickler records that a check was done and captures the evidence that it was: that a safer recruitment step was completed, that a policy was reviewed and current, that an observed practice matched the standard. It is not a child protection case-management system and it does not hold concerns, referrals or personal records about a child. When self-evaluation touches child protection, the nursery records that the process was followed and the evidence exists, without copying any child's personal information into quickler. The safeguarding record stays in your own child protection system as the single source of truth.</p>"
    },
