      "html": "<h3>What is nursery self-evaluation in Scotland?</h3><p>It is the process by which a Scottish nursery or early learning and childcare service judges its own quality against the Care Inspectorate framework How good is our early learning and childcare? and the Health and Social Care Standards, honestly and continuously, and evidences each judgement. It covers care, play and learning, the setting, the staff team including ratios and safeguarding, and leadership, graded on a six-point scale. Childcare in Scotland is regulated by the Care Inspectorate, not Ofsted, which covers England only, and not CQC.</p><h3>What is How good is our early learning and childcare?</h3><p>It is the Care Inspectorate's quality framework for early learning and childcare services, including nurseries and day care of children. It sets out the key questions and quality indicators an inspector uses and against which a service self-evaluates, and it is used alongside the Health and Social Care Standards. Always work from the current published framework, as the Care Inspectorate updates its guidance, and treat this page as general information, not regulatory advice.</p><h3>How does an early learning and childcare inspection work?</h3><p>The Care Inspectorate inspects against How good is our early learning and childcare? and the Health and Social Care Standards, grades key questions on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent, and looks at how honestly a service self-evaluates and acts on what it finds. A service that knows itself, evidences its judgements and can show live improvement work fares better than one filling in a form the week before. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector.</p><h3>Can I run nursery self-evaluation over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's workflow runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The manager or room lead receives each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat, replies with text, a voice note or a photo against each quality indicator, and the report and improvement plan generate automatically. No separate app or login is required, and no child's personal data is entered, because quickler is an audit and evidence tool, not a children's records or child protection system. Quickler is £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, with a £20 minimum, dormant users free. There is a free tier of 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/childminder-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Childminder self-evaluation Scotland</a></li></ul>"
